• Rose: Woody flowering plant with layered petals and a classic scent, commonly grown in red, pink, white, and yellow.
• Sunflower: Tall plant with a large yellow-petaled head and a seed-filled center that often tracks the sun.
• Lotus: Aquatic flower with broad, water-repellent leaves and blooms in shades of pink, white, or yellow.
• Tulip: Spring-blooming bulb flower with a smooth, cup- or bell-shaped bloom in many bright colors.
• Jasmine: Small, fragrant white or yellow blossoms often prized in perfumes, teas, and floral garlands.
